  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe 5.0.2 running-launcher guard over-corrected: it hard-blocked any install while a launcher was running, but that is the normal flow on POSIX (uv unlinks open files, so the running app keeps old code in memory and picks up the new version on restart). On Windows, uv cannot replace the tool environment while a process runs from it, so the fix is to **defer**, not refuse.\n\n### 1. `install.sh` — removed the running-launcher guard entirely\n\nPOSIX install-while-running is native and must keep working.\n\n### 2. `install.ps1` — detects running launchers and defers instead of refusing\n\nWhen any launcher is live, the installer stages the verified wheel and hands the install to a **detached PowerShell helper** that:\n- waits for those launchers to exit (bounded);\n- then runs `uv tool install --force` with backoff retry (same as the dashboard updater's deferred helper);\n- does **not** start the app — the user restarts it and picks up the new version.\n\nWhen no launcher is running, it installs directly as before.\n\n## Verification\n\nEnd-to-end on Windows, isolated tool dir:\n1. Launched `fcc-server` from the isolated bin.\n2. Ran the fixed `install.ps1` → it downloaded/verified v5.0.2, detected the running launcher, staged, and printed **\"Update staged for after restart\"** (no refusal, no `os error 32`).\n3. Stopped the launcher → the detached helper completed the install → the tool reported `free-claude-code 5.0.2`.\n\nFull suite: **16 failed / 3661 passed** — identical failure set to unmodified main (16 pre-existing PowerShell failures), zero regressions.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The deferred helper waits up to 6 hours for the launchers to exit; if they never stop, the install is not applied and the user is told to re-run the installer. The staged wheel is cleaned up after a successful install.\n- `Get-Process -Name` matches process names globally (not per bin-dir), which is the right scope — a running proxy child is what blocks uv regardless of which dir it launched from.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
