    "message": "fix: 5.0.3 restore install-while-running; Windows defers instead of refusing\n\nThe 5.0.2 running-launcher guard over-corrected: it hard-blocked any install\nwhile a launcher was running, but that is the normal flow on POSIX (uv unlinks\nopen files, so the running app keeps old code in memory and picks up the new\nversion on restart). On Windows, uv cannot replace the tool environment while a\nprocess runs from it, so the fix is to defer, not refuse.\n\n1. install.sh: removed the running-launcher guard entirely. POSIX\n   install-while-running is native and must keep working.\n\n2. install.ps1: detects running launchers and, when any are live, stages the\n   verified wheel and hands the install to a detached PowerShell helper that\n   waits for those launchers to exit, then runs uv tool install --force (with\n   backoff retry, same as the dashboard updater's deferred helper). It does not\n   start the app -- the user restarts it and picks up the new version. When no\n   launcher is running, it installs directly as before.\n\nVerified end-to-end on Windows: with a running fcc-server, the installer prints\n\"update staged for after restart\" (no refusal, no os error 32); after stopping\nthe launcher, the detached helper completed the install and the tool reported\nv5.0.2. Full suite 16 failed / 3661 passed -- identical failure set to\nunmodified main (16 pre-existing PowerShell failures), zero regressions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
